id: pm-ado-sdk-adoption
title: Use SDK settings-aware item reads and guarded sync persistence
description: "Adopt both unused SDK capabilities from the 2026-10-25 audit: settings-aware locateItem and commitItemMutations match preconditions. Preserve raw-document hashes and ordinary sync output; prove configured lookup and concurrent-write refusal with real non-git trackers, origin/main differential evidence and behavioural revert tests."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: refactor,sdk-adoption
created_at: "2026-10-25T16:11:56.608Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T08:04:08.572Z"
author: codex-agent
parent: pm-ado-g4v1
comments[61]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T15:50:43.902Z",codex-agent,"Orientation found no existing SDK-adoption item. Related SDK certification: pm-ado-qq1p; source features: pm-ado-4x3u and pm-ado-nc7z. Both audited SDK APIs exist in the pinned 2026.10.23 dependency. Plan: preserve authoritative raw documents, replace unguarded sync persistence with inspected-snapshot match preconditions, run non-git regression/differential/revert proofs and unchanged npm/Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-25T15:57:29.077Z",codex-agent,"Both replacements implemented. Resolution passes readSettings item_format and resolveItemTypeRegistry type_to_folder into locateItem and retains readLocatedItem whole-document hashing. Sync now uses commitItemMutations update match on inspected updated_at for link, relation and base writes. Expected revisions advance from our own immutable SDK transaction history, never from a refreshed current item. Three new real non-git regressions pass: custom nested folder/raw-document guard, local edit after Azure PATCH, and local edit before import relation/base persistence. The last two preserve the concurrent item/history bytes and return ADO_CONFLICT; remote success can remain partial."
  "2026-10-25T16:01:16.414Z",codex-agent,"Compatibility check found SDK gap tracked by pm-ado-sdk-match-close-1025: match on updated_at also runs inside update's internal terminal close after its first write has advanced the timestamp. Workaround uses one SDK transaction with a guarded scalar update then explicit close. SDK history messages necessarily become bulk-item-transaction markers instead of adapter prose; this intentional diagnostic difference is documented and differential-tested. Initial read-only differential passed over public pm-ado and pm-jira origin snapshots: 140 items, 8 exact output comparisons, unchanged authoritative bytes. Extending proof to writable copies for persistence receipts, values and history patches."
  "2026-10-25T16:03:28.536Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof, lookup: restored only AdoResolutionService.document from origin/main, rebuilt dist, then node --test --test-name-pattern='SDK lookup' test/sync.test.ts failed 1/1 as expected (custom nested folder scope refusal). Revert proof, sync: replaced only the local update helper with ordinary pm.update, rebuilt dist, then node --test --test-name-pattern='SDK sync match' test/sync.test.ts failed 2/2 as expected (newer local edits overwritten / success instead of conflict). Restored both implementations and rebuilt: all 4 targeted tests pass, including terminal lifecycle compatibility. No history records were rewritten."
  "2026-10-25T16:03:30.848Z",codex-agent,"Differential PASS: origin/main 7f44a1d build versus candidate, public pm-ado 7f44a1d (32 items) and pm-jira 2fd1537 (108 items). Four exact read-only outputs per corpus: import/export/sync dry-run and resolution plan, unchanged authoritative bytes. Three writable-copy persistence projections per corpus: actual import receipt, final metadata excluding updated_at, history op/author/patch excluding updated_at; history lengths equal. Total 14 comparisons over 140 real items. Only intentional difference in ordinary writes is mandatory SDK transaction history messages; both old/new forms asserted. Full method and reproducible command in docs/sdk-adoption.md."
  "2026-10-25T16:05:59.894Z",codex-agent,"Targeted compatibility checks passed 7/7. The first full gate ran 229/229 tests successfully but correctly rejected uncovered SDK error propagation (100% thresholds unchanged). Added a real-tracker regression for invalid mapped state and unusable transaction storage, plus explicit/unknown author attribution; it passes 1/1. Pinned pm linked tests passed 2/2 (typecheck and 4 targeted regressions); test-result tracking is disabled by existing project policy, so run output was inspected and results recorded here. Isolated-identity strict health passes. Normal host health exposes an unrelated global pm-github host-version skew; no global config was changed."
  "2026-10-25T16:09:54.868Z",codex-agent,"Local npm full gate PASS: env HOME=an isolated home GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check (the HOME expression here is descriptive only; run used an isolated home). Both the V8 pass and independent statement-instrumented pass ran 230/230 tests, 0 failures/skips. All 8 required source files covered; 1380/1380 statements, 100% lines/branches/functions; docstrings 90/90 declarations, production audit zero vulnerabilities, build/typecheck/pack/changelog/publish-attestation/date checks passed. git diff --check clean. No standalone lint script exists in this repository; its configured docstring gate passed. Bun full gate is running."
  "2026-10-25T16:15:34.693Z",codex-agent,"Local full gates PASS: env HOME=\"$(mktemp -d)\" GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check; the same isolated identity with bun run release:check also passes. Each gate runs 230/230 tests in both V8 and independent statement-instrumented passes, with zero failures/skips. Coverage: 1380/1380 statements and 100% lines/branches/functions across 8 sources. Typecheck/build, 90/90 documented declarations, production audit zero vulnerabilities, pack/changelog/attestation/date checks pass. Pinned pm linked tests rerun on this item: 2/2 pass. Public text privacy scan and git diff --check pass. No standalone lint script is configured. Ready for PR CI; no merge or release authorized."
  "2026-10-25T16:20:11.498Z",codex-agent,"First published head ddb45e2 CI passed all four jobs: Node 22, Node 26, npm release gate and Bun release gate; https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/40210848558 . Each coverage pass ran 230/230 tests, zero failures/skips, four 100% coverage dimensions. Final compatibility inspection found that transaction author selection should also reuse core precedence: now uses selectImportAuthor with readSettings.author_default so configured authors survive when neither explicit author nor PM_AUTHOR is set. Targeted lookup/race/terminal/error/configured-author checks pass 5/5. Sync revert repeated after this adjustment: both race tests fail under ordinary pm.update; restored and rebuilt. Final differential repeated: 14 comparisons across 140 public items pass. Local full gates are rerunning for the final code. Automated review statuses are not approvals: review services reported quota/trial/configuration limits; no substantive inline findings."
  "2026-10-25T16:31:57.103Z",codex-agent,"Final code full gates PASS: isolated-identity npm run release:check and bun run release:check both completed successfully. Each ran 230/230 tests in both V8 and independent statement-instrumented passes, zero failures/skips, all four coverage dimensions 100% across 8 required sources; statements 1381/1381. Typecheck/build, docstrings 90/90 declarations, audit zero vulnerabilities, pack/changelog/attestation/date checks pass. Final direct lookup/race/terminal/error/configured-author regression command passes 5/5; pinned pm linked commands rerun 2/2. Differential rerun: 14 comparisons over 140 public items pass. Lookup revert fails 1/1; final sync helper revert fails 2/2; replacements restored and rebuilt. SDK persistence conflicts (including lock/ownership refusals) intentionally use ADO_CONFLICT; history markers and custom-folder support are documented. PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/pull/46 is ready for review; first CI run passed 4/4 jobs and final-head CI is linked at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/pull/46/checks . SDK follow-up pm-ado-sdk-match-close-1025 remains open for orchestrator reporting. No live Azure credentials were used. Releasing this claim for orchestrator verification; items remain unclosed."
  "2026-10-25T19:48:44.999Z",codex-agent,"Reopened for blocking review on PR 46. Preserve completed lookup/differential work. Close both classes: conditional local mutation sequences including lifecycle transitions, and durable idempotent/recoverable Azure side effects. Add real interleaving/process-crash matrix with a recording REST fixture, behavioural revert proofs, and full npm/Bun CI gates. Existing SDK terminal-match gap will be revisited; no thread replies or upstream issue writes."
  "2026-10-25T20:03:36.893Z",codex-agent,"Blocking cases now pass on real non-git trackers. Closing is a scalar update then a status-only update, each commitItemMutations update carrying the revision from our previous immutable history event; no unguarded close remains. Durable scoped outbox intents precede Azure create/PATCH, with creation keys derived from local id + operation + original plan and stamped in reserved Azure tags. Retry resolves the marker before creation and preserves local edits when completing a failed link. PATCH carries a revision assertion and history marker. A recording REST/interleaving/real SIGKILL matrix is running. Provider limitation: ambiguous create dispatch with no visible marker must fail closed to avoid a second POST; automatic convergence in that ambiguous case requires a server uniqueness guarantee not present in the documented Work Item Create API. Clarification requested while remaining work continues."
  "2026-10-25T20:42:16.310Z",codex-agent,"Review revert proof, local commits: reverted only the update grouping function to a matched scalar commit followed by an unguarded SDK close. Rebuilt. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"blocking review: a local status\" test/sync.test.ts failed 1/1: success/closed replaced the concurrently blocked status. Restored and rebuilt. The fix uses two matched update mutations, the second status-only, carrying forward our own preceding revision."
  "2026-10-25T20:42:17.547Z",codex-agent,"Review revert proof, creation: reverted only SyncOutbox.create to a direct Azure create call. Rebuilt. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"blocking review: local edits during Azure create\" test/sync.test.ts failed 1/1 because retry allocated another remote object. Restored and rebuilt. Durable first-plan intent, exact marker lookup and refusal to redispatch an ambiguous create prevent another POST."
  "2026-10-25T20:42:18.612Z",codex-agent,"Review revert proof, PATCH effects: reverted only SyncOutbox.patch to direct revision-checked PATCH. Rebuilt. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"conditional outbox PATCH replay\" test/sync.test.ts failed all 4 leaf cases (5 failed tests including the parent): no durable recovery/marker proof, lost response cannot replay, and protocol tags are not preserved. Restored and rebuilt."
  "2026-10-25T20:42:19.873Z",codex-agent,"Review revert proof, import pairing: reverted only SyncOutbox.owners to an empty ownership result. Rebuilt. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"sync reconnects its own pending export\" test/sync.test.ts failed 1/1: the created remote object was imported as another local item instead of reconnecting the original. Restored and rebuilt. Ownership and the original/accepted creation snapshots are now consulted before pairing, including partially linked records."
  "2026-10-25T20:42:20.970Z",codex-agent,"Review progress: all five expanded boundary scenarios passed (terminal import, fresh export, relation export, recovery export, mixed sync). These enumerate REST, local SDK commit and intent-write boundaries with real edits and SIGKILL. Ambiguous create-dispatch cases explicitly hold without another POST until the original marker becomes visible. The separate 412 CLI regression exposed an incomplete fake-server revision feed, which was corrected; its focused rerun passes 1/1. Both production modules reached 100% lines/functions; one redundant close-reason fallback branch was removed by supplying the reason at the configured close-status call site. Full unchanged coverage gates are next. Restored fixed/replay/ownership test command passes after all four reverts."
  "2026-10-25T21:19:44.401Z",codex-agent,"Review revert proof, prior PATCH reconciliation: reverted only SyncOutbox.bases to return no recovered base. Rebuilt. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"SDK sync match refuses a local edit after Azure PATCH\" test/sync.test.ts failed 1/1 because retry treated its own accepted Azure change as a competing edit and could not converge. Restored. The recovery reader proves operation markers at exact historical revisions and reconciles multiple accepted effects in order. A separate regression covers two successive mapped local edits, preserves both latest title and body, and settles with exactly three PATCHes and a subsequent no-op."
  "2026-10-25T21:19:50.172Z",codex-agent,"Provider constraint remains unresolved: the documented Azure Work Item Create API has no server-enforced idempotency key or unique-tag precondition. A crash between durable dispatch and actual POST cannot guarantee both zero duplicates and automatic convergence. Implementation preserves the intent, retries exact marker lookup, and refuses another POST while the outcome is unknown. The orchestrator was asked whether fail-closed recovery is acceptable or a uniqueness service exists; no approval has been assumed. Crash tests explicitly distinguish this held state from convergence after provider visibility. No live Azure call was made."
  "2026-10-25T21:24:39.988Z",codex-agent,"Final source revalidation: all five function-only behavioural reverts fail as expected (close 1/1, create 1/1, PATCH 4/4 leaf cases plus parent, ownership 1/1, accepted-base recovery 1/1); restored focused cases pass 11/11. Latest six fixed/repeated-edit/concurrent-process regressions pass 6/6 through pm test --run --only-last --progress. Typecheck, 92 documented declarations, whitespace, public-path privacy scan and append-only history checks pass."
  "2026-10-25T21:24:42.367Z",codex-agent,"Final differential after all review repairs: 14/14 comparisons across read-only non-git copies of 140 real public tracker items pass against origin/main 7f44a1d (pm-ado 32, pm-jira 108). Dry-run receipts and authoritative bytes match. Writable-copy import receipts, values and history patches match after normalizing mutation timestamps; mandatory SDK history markers remain the only exercised history-message difference. Public source snapshots are never modified or committed. Full npm/Bun release checks are running with isolated Git identity and unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-25T21:36:00.122Z",codex-agent,"Final V8 full-suite pass: 423/423 tests, zero failures/skips, all nine required source files at 100% lines, branches and functions. The 164 matrix fault cells passed (82 real edits and 82 actual SIGKILL interruptions across five scenarios). Independent statement coverage is still running; complete npm/Bun release-gate evidence will be appended separately. Repair code and current PM history are grouped in one commit; the Bun gate will use a clean detached checkout of that exact commit to keep build outputs isolated."
  "2026-10-25T21:45:21.508Z",codex-agent,"Repair commit a735bd1 passed full CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/40236418608 . All 4 jobs (Node 22, Node 26, npm release gate, Bun release gate) succeeded. Every job ran 423/423 tests in both V8 and independent statement passes, zero failures/skips. All 9 required sources: 1580/1580 statements and 100% lines/branches/functions. CodeQL also passed: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/40236418649 . This is the requested full-gate evidence; duplicate local release runs were interrupted after CI completed and are not counted as successful local full gates. Completed local full V8 pass was 423/423 at 100% lines/branches/functions; latest linked targeted command 6/6, restored revert cases 11/11, typecheck and 92 documented declarations passed. No standalone lint script exists."
  "2026-10-25T21:45:23.842Z",codex-agent,"Final review matrix: 82 observed boundaries, 164 fault cells (82 actual local edits and 82 real worker SIGKILL interruptions) across terminal import, fresh export, relation export, pending-export recovery and mixed sync. All passed in both CI coverage passes. Both reported races are fixed. Repeated mapped edits after PATCH also converge using ordered historical operation proofs; independent exporter processes allocate one remote identity. Remaining acceptance limit is the documented ambiguous-create dispatch state: no second POST is issued, but an actually unsent request cannot automatically converge without an additional provider uniqueness/recovery contract. No approval to resend has been assumed. SDK terminal-match API gap remains on pm-ado-sdk-match-close-1025 for orchestrator reporting. Releasing adoption claim for verification; neither item is closed."
  "2026-10-26T03:25:17.263Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 review reopened: keep completed SDK adoption and first-round proofs. Fix base publication order so a crash between scalar update and terminal close cannot make sync reverse Azure. Complete the outbox outcome state machine, including definitive rejections and corrected-plan retries. Add semantic SIGKILL convergence assertions using the next sync, deterministic randomized fake-Azure model coverage, both fixed cases and function-only revert proofs. Targeted/typecheck/docstring checks locally; unchanged npm/Bun CI release gates. No merge, mentions or thread replies."
  "2026-10-26T03:48:22.873Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 implementation: terminal sync now commits scalars without ado_sync_base/ado_rev, then a matched status-only close, then agreement/revision publication last against the close revision. Non-terminal fields and their base stay in one conditional SDK update. All relation operations finish before publication. The fixed SIGKILL case restarts with ordinary sync and preserves Closed on both sides; every reopening PATCH is forbidden. Native SDK close clears assignment, so the settled crash oracle includes that existing lifecycle policy rather than incorrectly requiring zero PATCHes."
  "2026-10-26T03:48:24.904Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 outbox: one total state/event table and executor now own prepared, dispatched, observed and rejected. Typed AdoHttpError preserves response status; definitive 4xx except 408 and revision refusals become rejected. Only durable rejection permits corrected type/fields/projection/key to replace a create plan. 5xx, 408, invalid JSON and connection/timeout failures retain unknown dispatch and resolve original markers/history before retry. Successful lookup/historical proof is durably observed; a proven foreign PATCH revision becomes rejected. Unknown creation still cannot blindly resend."
  "2026-10-26T03:48:26.781Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 targeted command passed 17/17 tests: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"round-2|conditional outbox PATCH replay|pending PATCH bases|blocking review|successive mapped edits\" test/sync.test.ts . Seeded model: 36 create sequences, 53 definitive rejections corrected, 16 ambiguous outcomes held until provider visibility, 36 unique observed identities; 33 PATCH sequences, 14 definitive refusals retried, exactly 33 accepted revisions/unique links/history effects. Three real SIGKILL rejection boundaries distinguish durable rejection from lost proof. Typecheck/build/test-typecheck and 98 documented declarations pass; whitespace check clean. Complete semantic crash matrix and source coverage are running."
  "2026-10-26T03:55:24.579Z",codex-agent,"Additional total-state correction: a never-dispatched prepared plan may safely refresh to current inputs after looking up its old marker. Retaining stale prepared fields could otherwise overwrite a mapped local edit after an interruption before dispatch. The new real-tracker regression changes title, body and Azure type before retry and proves one creation with the latest input. Unknown dispatched and observed plans remain immutable. Semantic crash matrix passed 196 fault cells across six scenarios, including terminal import and terminal export, using next ordinary sync and assertions against every reopening PATCH."
  "2026-10-26T03:56:54.111Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 revert proof, base ordering: restored only the local update grouping function from e677059 and rebuilt. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"round-2 fixed case: SIGKILL\" test/sync.test.ts failed 1/1: next ordinary sync reopened Azure to New instead of preserving Closed. Restored the function and rebuilt. Agreement/revision publication now follows the durable close, with every commit matched to the preceding revision."
  "2026-10-26T03:56:56.596Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 revert proof, outcome classification: reverted only SyncOutbox.execute to dispatch, call and success recording without the failure transition. Rebuilt. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"round-2 fixed case: definitive\" test/sync.test.ts failed 1/1 because corrected export remained ADO_CONFLICT after HTTP 400. Restored and rebuilt. Definitive rejection is now durably recorded; ambiguous failures retain the original dispatch key."
  "2026-10-26T03:56:58.245Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 revert proof, corrected plans: disabled only the safe replan branch inside SyncOutbox.create and rebuilt. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"round-2 fixed case: definitive\" test/sync.test.ts failed 1/1 because the rejected plan could not accept corrected input. Restored and rebuilt. Latest focused command passes 18/18, including changed inputs before any dispatch, both fixed cases, 69 seeded sequences, PATCH replay, and three real rejection-response/journal crash boundaries. Pinned pm linked run previously passed 17/17 before the added prepared-input case; the new restored command includes it. No SDK version or thresholds changed."
  "2026-10-26T03:58:12.267Z",codex-agent,"Final round-2 source diagnostic: both sync.ts and sync-outbox.ts reach 100% lines, branches and functions with the full non-matrix regression selection; the separate six-scenario semantic matrix passed 196 fault cells. Final differential against recorded origin baseline 7f44a1d passes 14/14 comparisons across 140 public items. Typecheck, test typecheck, 98 documented declarations, changelog and whitespace checks pass. CI remains the full four-dimension npm/Bun release-gate evidence. Preparing one repair commit with PM records, then incorporating the newer main release-policy commit before CI; no SDK dependency change."
  "2026-10-26T04:14:42.734Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 complete repair CI PASS on merged head 9fe7628 (repair 4c29583 plus current main): https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/40266894633 . All 4 jobs succeeded: Node 22, Node 26, npm release gate and Bun release gate. Each job ran 469/469 tests in both V8 and independent statement passes, zero failures/skips. All four coverage dimensions 100% across 9 required sources; statements 1607/1607. CodeQL passed: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/40266894638 . Unchanged thresholds and SDK pin. Final pinned pm linked run passes 18/18; local non-matrix diagnostic 83/83 with both sync modules at 100% lines/branches/functions. Typecheck, test typecheck, 98 documented declarations, changelog, strict health, privacy, whitespace and history-prefix checks pass. No standalone lint script exists."
  "2026-10-26T04:14:44.022Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 final evidence: base and acknowledged revision publish LAST after guarded native close; non-terminal values/base stay one conditional commit. Six scenarios cover 98 observed boundaries and 196 edit/SIGKILL cells, restarting with ordinary sync and rejecting transient reopening PATCHes. Three additional real rejection crash boundaries distinguish durable rejected state from lost proof. Seeded model: 36 create sequences (53 definitive rejections corrected, 16 unknown outcomes held until provider proof, 36 unique observed identities) and 33 PATCH sequences (14 refusals retried; 33 unique accepted revisions/links/history effects). Three function-only behavioral reverts each fail 1/1; restored focused command passes 18/18. Differential remains 14/14 comparisons across 140 public tracker items. Unknown creates, including rejection responses lost before journaling or older dispatched records without proof, still require provider visibility/uniqueness or an explicit recovery contract; no blind resend is allowed or approved. Releasing adoption claim for orchestrator verification; both PM items remain unclosed."
  "2026-10-26T23:34:27.666Z",codex-agent,"Re-review reopened for the three-way merge BASE class. Replace whole accepted-remote recovery promotion with per-key effect provenance; only post-operation local/Azure read-back agreement may advance stored base or acknowledged revision. Consolidate all base/revision writes, including resolution, behind one function. Add the reproduced scalar-PATCH/remote-link interruption plus a >=500-sequence two-writer reference model, retain earlier fixed cases, perform model revert proof, and run targeted/typecheck/docstring checks plus unchanged npm/Bun CI gates. Local tests use at most two workers; no concurrent full suites. No merge, mentions or thread replies."
  "2026-10-26T23:47:53.846Z",codex-agent,"R3 implementation progress: recovery now carries owned scalar-effect provenance instead of promoting the accepted remote snapshot into a base. A new advanceSyncBase function reads the actual SDK tracker and expanded Azure object after operations, advances only equal keys, and acknowledges a revision only on full agreement. Actual local relation projection is independent of remote snapshots. Sync and resolution base/revision publication both delegate to this function; early link/create acknowledgments were removed. Remaining unequal keys yield typed conflict. Partial initial bases explicitly mark unknown keys. Native close runs through the SDK, followed by an explicit SDK assignment update when needed so successful import has equal mapped values. Installed SDK declarations and upstream open issues were searched: commitWorkspaceTransaction exists; BulkItemCloseMutation still has no match signature. No acceptance is being deferred as an SDK gap. Focused cases compile; model/review regression and full validation are next."
  "2026-10-27T00:11:10.386Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 fixed case now retains a remote relation across interruption immediately after scalar PATCH. Sync and resolution publish only through advanceSyncBase using actual local graph and expanded Azure read-back; recovery proof is limited to scalar keys actually sent and never substitutes an accepted snapshot for common base. Added a deterministic 512-sequence two-sided model with native SDK trackers, recording Azure server, interruption/resume and further edits; validating its independent edit ledger now. Existing SDK pin and all coverage thresholds are unchanged."
  "2026-10-27T00:18:14.250Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 differential passes 14/14 comparisons over 140 public items in two non-git read-only snapshot corpora, with writable copies for import. Receipts, values and net history patches match the original main build. Intentional history differences are guarded SDK transaction messages, patch path ordering and a separate final agreement event (two events instead of one). Strict isolated-identity health passes; only the existing advisory telemetry queue is reported and no telemetry configuration was touched. Typecheck and 111/111 documented declarations pass. The 512-sequence model caught a test misuse of strict SDK dependency removal (selectors for absent edges), now corrected to remove only existing rows."
  "2026-10-27T00:27:09.791Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 behavioural revert proof: revert ONLY mergeSyncValues so owned recovery assigns base = effect.accepted (the whole accepted Azure snapshot). Command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"round-3 model\" test/sync.test.ts. Result: 0/1 pass, 1/1 fail in the reference model reviewed-case prefix: expected the remote relation count 1, observed 0 (recovery erased an unimported remote edit). Restored the function immediately; dedicated fixed case passes. No SDK or test fixture was replaced for the revert. The full 512-sequence run and complete gates remain in progress."
  "2026-10-27T00:37:33.905Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 restored targeted checks pass 13/13. advanceSyncBase and readBaseRevisions have 100% V8 lines, branches and functions in that focused run. Added per-key witnessed Azure revisions inside the base so acknowledged scalar proof is retired independently when unrelated relations still prevent a whole-item revision acknowledgement. A dedicated reference test requires a typed conflict for later competing scalar edits despite an older owned effect. recoverEffects now names its returned original/accepted request evidence explicitly; it never returns or publishes common base. Added real SIGKILL matrices for simultaneous local scalar/remote relation edits and pending-PATCH recovery, covering all observed REST/local/outbox boundaries. New matrices and the 512-sequence run are in progress."
  "2026-10-27T00:45:23.221Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 real-process acceptance passes 62/62 tests: 60 edit/SIGKILL fault cells plus two scenario parents, over 30 observed boundaries in simultaneous scalar/link sync and pending PATCH recovery. Both new matrices check settled intended values, preserved annotations, unique remote and local identities and replay with no additional creation. Final differential passes 14/14 across 140 public items with only documented history grouping, transaction markers, path ordering and internal per-key revision coordinates differing. Pinned pm test --run --progress linked selections pass 5/5 fixed cases and 4/4 agreement contracts. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstrings and changelog pass. The inherited 500-sequence normalization model passed 500 sequences, 500 exact replays and 50 stale replays; the new two-sided 512-sequence model and package-wide local regression selection are still running. CI npm/Bun release gates will provide complete exact-head coverage evidence."
  "2026-10-27T01:16:52.561Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 local model completed: seed 0x37a9c521, 512 sequences, 230 interrupted commands, 444 converged retries and 68 typed conflicts. All scalar/relationship actor categories were exercised on both sides; successful syncs matched actual stores and every published base key had an equality witness. This is the first local model receipt; full CI reruns the complete model on its exact checkout. Final-head function-only proofs each fail 1/1: promoting the accepted snapshot deletes the remote link (0 instead of 1), and removing per-key proof retirement chooses remote instead of reporting a competing scalar conflict. Restored agreement contracts pass 4/4. Added two caller regressions, both passing: native SDK validation leaves item/base untouched; scalar resolution publishes only matching scalar keys, leaves an unimported link out of base and allows ordinary sync plus replay without another PATCH. Broad local selection passes 288/289; only packed-install setup fails because npm registry metadata fetch times out, reproduced in isolation. Curl can reach the public registry; no host network configuration changed. CI run 40428452207 is running the full npm/Bun release gates and Node matrix."
  "2026-10-27T01:55:56.637Z",codex-agent,"Full CI exposed three additional cases beyond the focused BASE regressions: native close transiently clears assignment before mapped completion; later PATCH proof replaced unrelated creation-default proof; and a manually unlinked copied extension cannot resolve guarded SDK primitives. Repair now journals package-owned local plans through matched SDK mutations before every local effect, distinguishes latest foreign edits per synced key using SDK immutable history, resumes only proven native-close assignment, and clears the plan in the same conditional agreement commit. Recovery retains every owned request and selects proof per key. Proper SDK links remain required; manual unlinking gets an explicit dependency refusal rather than weaker local mutation logic. Host facade limitation is tracked by pm-ado-host-sdk-facade. Initial repaired smoke passes 8/8; all affected close/create recovery fault boundaries are being rerun."
  "2026-10-27T03:17:00.145Z",codex-agent,"Current repair evidence: 87/87 close/create-recovery matrix and reversion tests pass; 9/9 new local-intent, SDK-link, inverse-endpoint and bidirectional-reversion checks pass; 14/14 differential comparisons over 140 public items pass with three guarded local-history events instead of one. Five final function-only reverts each fail 1/1: whole-snapshot base promotion; missing per-key proof retirement; latest-request-only proof; ignoring a foreign scalar reversion; and skipping native-close assignment recovery. Restoring them passes the selected regressions. The first complete local model ran 512 sequences with seed 0x37a9c521, 230 interruptions, 444 converged retries and 68 typed conflicts; complete exact-head CI reruns it. Local plans retain actual remote identity/revision bounds, and the agreement function refuses revisions older than any previously witnessed key. Native SDK validation may add an intent receipt but preserves synced data and the prior base. Local npm packed acceptance remains blocked by registry timeouts; CI exercises real package launchers. No SDK pin or coverage threshold was changed."
  "2026-10-27T03:27:43.539Z",codex-agent,"Exact source head 0ac2505: Node 26 CI passed 663/663 behavioral tests with zero failures/skips, including all eight edit/SIGKILL matrices and the two-sided reference model (512 sequences; seed 0x37a9c521; 278 interruptions, 408 converged retries, 104 typed conflicts). The gate correctly refused 99.80% aggregate branch coverage: resolution 99.63%, sync 99.45%; every source line and function is covered. Adding focused missing-branch cases before repeating the unchanged full npm/Bun gates. CI run: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/40443350385 ."
